Below is a quick mapping of the columns that matter for the requested report, followed by ten exploratory / incremental Snowflake queries (each limited to 20 rows) that walk from simple inspection to the final analytical‐style query.  
All identifiers are enclosed in double quotes exactly as they exist in the catalog.

Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• ORDERS."order_id":            primary key that ties to ORDER_ITEMS."order_id" – counts “orders”  
• ORDERS."created_at":          order creation time‑stamp (µs since epoch) – used to assign orders to months  
• ORDER_ITEMS."order_id":       foreign key – links items back to orders  
• ORDER_ITEMS."product_id":     foreign key – joins to PRODUCTS."id" for category & cost  
• ORDER_ITEMS."sale_price":     revenue generated by the individual item  
• ORDER_ITEMS."created_at":     alternate time‑stamp; usually same as order’s  
• PRODUCTS."id":                primary key for products  
• PRODUCTS."category":          product category needed in the report  
• PRODUCTS."cost":              unit cost – profit = sale_price – cost  
• (OPTIONAL) ORDERS."status"/ORDER_ITEMS."status": we keep all statuses but they’re good for filtering tests

Key time window conditions (micro‑seconds)  
• start_of_june_2019     = 1559347200000000  
• end_of_dec_2019        = 1577836800000000  

Ten sample queries  
(Queries 1‑3 are “sanity checks”, 4‑6 show joins and simple aggregates, 7‑10 become increasingly complex up to the final answer‑style query.)

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at a few orders created in 2019 to confirm the time‑stamp domain.
SELECT "order_id",
       "created_at",
       "status"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"
WHERE  "created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000  -- 2019‑06‑01
                       AND 1577836800000000    -- 2020‑01‑01
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Get distinct months (yyyy‑mm) present in ORDER_ITEMS during 2019.
SELECT DISTINCT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP("created_at"/1e6), 'YYYY‑MM') AS "month"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"
WHERE  "created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1577836800000000
ORDER  BY "month"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: List a sample of product categories in use.
SELECT DISTINCT "category"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Join ORDER_ITEMS to PRODUCTS to see revenue vs. cost per line.
SELECT oi."order_id",
       oi."product_id",
       p."category",
       oi."sale_price",
       p."cost",
       oi."sale_price" - p."cost" AS "profit"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"      p
       ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE  oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1577836800000000
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Aggregate revenue & profit per order per month (all statuses kept).
SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at"/1e6), 'YYYY‑MM') AS "month",
       oi."order_id",
       SUM(oi."sale_price")              AS "order_revenue",
       SUM(oi."sale_price" - p."cost")   AS "order_profit"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"      p
       ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE  oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1577836800000000
GROUP  BY 1, 2
ORDER  BY 1, 2
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Count total orders by month (using ORDERS table).
SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP("created_at"/1e6), 'YYYY‑MM') AS "month",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "order_id")                         AS "orders_cnt"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"
WHERE  "created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1577836800000000
GROUP  BY 1
ORDER  BY 1
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Combine item‑level revenue & profit per category per month.
SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at"/1e6), 'YYYY‑MM') AS "month",
       p."category",
       COUNT(DISTINCT oi."order_id")                         AS "orders_cnt",
       SUM(oi."sale_price")                                  AS "revenue",
       SUM(oi."sale_price" - p."cost")                       AS "profit"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"     p
       ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE  oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1577836800000000
GROUP  BY 1, 2
ORDER  BY 1, 2
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Add month‑over‑month (MoM) growth rates using June 2019 as base.
--        (Growth columns will be NULL for July calculations if June data absent.)
WITH m AS (
  SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at"/1e6), 'YYYY‑MM') AS "month",
         p."category",
         COUNT(DISTINCT oi."order_id")                         AS "orders_cnt",
         SUM(oi."sale_price")                                  AS "revenue",
         SUM(oi."sale_price" - p."cost")                       AS "profit"
  FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
  JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"     p
         ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
  WHERE  oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1577836800000000
  GROUP  BY 1, 2
)
SELECT "month",
       "category",
       "orders_cnt",
       "revenue",
       "profit",
       ROUND(("orders_cnt" / NULLIF(LAG("orders_cnt") OVER (PARTITION BY "category" ORDER BY "month"),0) - 1)*100,2) AS "orders_mom_%", 
       ROUND(("revenue"     / NULLIF(LAG("revenue")     OVER (PARTITION BY "category" ORDER BY "month"),0) - 1)*100,2) AS "revenue_mom_%",
       ROUND(("profit"      / NULLIF(LAG("profit")      OVER (PARTITION BY "category" ORDER BY "month"),0) - 1)*100,2) AS "profit_mom_%"
FROM   m
ORDER  BY "month", "category"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Filter out June 2019 from the final display but still reference it in MoM calculations.
WITH base AS (
  SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at"/1e6), 'YYYY‑MM') AS "month",
         p."category",
         COUNT(DISTINCT oi."order_id")                         AS "orders_cnt",
         SUM(oi."sale_price")                                  AS "revenue",
         SUM(oi."sale_price" - p."cost")                       AS "profit"
  FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
  JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"     p
         ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
  WHERE  oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1577836800000000
  GROUP  BY 1, 2
)
SELECT *
FROM   (
  SELECT "month",
         "category",
         "orders_cnt",
         "revenue",
         "profit",
         ROUND(("orders_cnt" / NULLIF(LAG("orders_cnt") OVER (PARTITION BY "category" ORDER BY "month"),0) - 1)*100,2) AS "orders_mom_%", 
         ROUND(("revenue"     / NULLIF(LAG("revenue")     OVER (PARTITION BY "category" ORDER BY "month"),0) - 1)*100,2) AS "revenue_mom_%",
         ROUND(("profit"      / NULLIF(LAG("profit")      OVER (PARTITION BY "category" ORDER BY "month"),0) - 1)*100,2) AS "profit_mom_%"
  FROM   base
) z
WHERE  z."month" <> '2019‑06'
ORDER  BY z."month", z."category"
LIMIT  20;
```

